UNIT diff_hint
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/lib/profile.mts diffHint (lines 76-100) and INVISIBLE (line 78, from cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs
  GLUE, line 73), driven through seams/diff_hint.mjs with both sides as UTF-8 text
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG diff_hint(existing: text, profile: text) -> text
ENVELOPE two well-formed texts (Unicode scalar values; a lone surrogate is out). Every such pair is in scope; there is no
  error path, and every result is well-formed text. Non-text arguments are out of the envelope.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION The one-line "what differs" hint rdv init --refresh prints for a tools/ script that differs from the
  profile's copy: the first line where the two disagree (a line one side lacks counts), the first column where the
  lines differ, and an escaped window of each side's line from that column; or a fixed sentence when the texts are equal.
  Every count and position below is in CODE POINTS (Unicode scalar values), never bytes, UTF-16 units or graphemes.
BEHAVIOR
R1 Each text is split into lines on U+000A (LINE FEED) only. Every other character, U+000D, U+2028, U+2029 and U+FEFF
  included, is ordinary line content. A text with k line feeds has k + 1 lines; the empty text is one empty line, and a
  text ending in a line feed ends with an empty line.
R2 Lines are visited at the same index from index 0 up to the larger line count; the FIRST index where the two sides
  disagree decides, with i its 0-based index. They disagree when one side has no line at i (R3) or both have one and
  the two lines are different sequences of code points (R4).
R3 MISSING LINE. When existing has no line i -> "line " + decimal(i + 1) + ": existing has no line " + decimal(i + 1) +
  ", profile has " + WINDOW(the profile line, 0). Symmetrically, when profile has no line i -> "line " + decimal(i + 1) +
  ": profile has no line " + decimal(i + 1) + ", existing has " + WINDOW(the existing line, 0). Since each side has at
  least one line, i >= 1 here. A trailing line feed on one side only is reported this way (the present line is empty).
R4 DIFFERING LINES. c = the length of the longest common prefix of the two lines in code points (0-based; c never exceeds
  the shorter line's length). Result -> "line " + decimal(i + 1) + ", col " + decimal(c + 1) + ": existing " +
  WINDOW(the existing line, c) + " vs profile " + WINDOW(the profile line, c).
R5 EQUAL. When no index disagrees (the texts are identical) -> the text
  "binary difference (the texts decode to the same UTF-8)". CITED FIDELITY package
R6 WINDOW(s, c) for a line s of L code points = QUOTE, then ELLIPSIS when c > 0, then ESCAPE of each code point of s at
  positions c up to but excluding min(c + WIDTH, L), in order, then ELLIPSIS when c + WIDTH < L, then QUOTE. When c = L the
  middle is empty: the shorter side of a prefix pair renders as QUOTE ELLIPSIS QUOTE when c > 0. The two ELLIPSIS marks are
  added, never escaped; WIDTH counts source code points, not the escaped length.
R7 ESCAPE maps one code point to text by the first row of TABLE ESCAPE that applies. Escapes are per code point and
  context-free; hex digits are lowercase; the four-digit and braced forms are chosen by the row. The window is a
  supplementary character's whole encoding or none of it (positions are code points), but a cut may fall inside a
  grapheme: between regional indicators, before a combining mark, a variation selector or a zero width joiner. CITED FIDELITY package
TABLE ESCAPE — code point -> text (R7); first row that applies
  U+0022 QUOTATION MARK                      -> backslash, then U+0022
  U+005C REVERSE SOLIDUS                     -> two backslashes
  U+0008                                     -> backslash, "b"
  U+0009                                     -> backslash, "t"
  U+000C                                     -> backslash, "f"
  U+000D                                     -> backslash, "r"
  any other code point U+0000 through U+001F -> backslash, "u", four lowercase hex digits of the code point
  a code point in INVISIBLE at or below U+FFFF -> backslash, "u", four lowercase hex digits of the code point
  a code point in INVISIBLE above U+FFFF     -> backslash, "u", "{", the lowercase hex digits of the code point with no
                                                leading zero (five here), "}"
  anything else                              -> the code point itself, unchanged
PINNED charset INVISIBLE = { U+000A..U+000D, U+007F..U+00A0, U+00AD, U+034F, U+0600..U+0605, U+061C, U+06DD, U+070F,
  U+0890, U+0891, U+08E2, U+115F, U+1160, U+1680, U+180B..U+180E, U+2000..U+200F, U+2028..U+202F, U+205F..U+2064,
  U+2066..U+206F, U+2800, U+3000, U+3164, U+FE00..U+FE0F, U+FEFF, U+FFA0, U+FFF9..U+FFFB, U+110BD, U+110CD,
  U+13430..U+1343F, U+1BCA0..U+1BCA3, U+1D173..U+1D17A, U+E0001, U+E0020..U+E007F, U+E0100..U+E01EF } CITED FIDELITY
  package — profile.mts line 78: the parser's pinned GLUE set (Unicode White_Space other than space and tab, and
  General_Category Cf, as of Unicode 17.0, never the host's tables) plus U+007F..U+009F, U+034F, U+115F, U+1160,
  U+180B..U+180D, U+2800, U+3164, U+FE00..U+FE0F, U+FFA0, U+E0100..U+E01EF; inclusive ranges, matched per code point.
  U+000A..U+000D never reach this row (U+000A splits lines, the C0 rows precede it). NOTHING outside it is escaped: U+2065,
  U+180F, U+17B4, U+17B5, U+FFF0..U+FFF8, U+E0000, U+E0002..U+E001F, U+E0080..U+E00FF, U+E01F0 and up, U+2026, U+FFFD, the
  solidus and combining marks are copied raw
PINNED text ELLIPSIS = U+2026 HORIZONTAL ELLIPSIS (one code point, bytes E2 80 A6) CITED R6
PINNED text QUOTE = U+0022 QUOTATION MARK CITED R6
PINNED number WIDTH = 80 code points CITED R6
INVARIANT the result never contains U+000A, U+000D or any other code point U+0000..U+001F: every window is a slice of one
  line and TABLE ESCAPE rewrites the rest.
INVARIANT decimal = base-10 digits of a positive integer, no sign, no separators, no leading zero.
ORACLE value -> oracles/diff_hint.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 ec5493378df84c44c0e2ef7a2b659325aeaa76894e11a5ccf785f7f757198a68
SCOPE IN: diffHint's computation over two texts, R1-R7. OUT: the caller's byte comparison and the decision to call it
  (applyProfile, profile.mts); the Buffer-to-text decode (the seam passes text, so invalid UTF-8 never arrives; the real
  code decodes each invalid sequence to U+FFFD, so two byte-different files can reach R5's sentence).
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 (MIT), cli/lib/profile.mts, function diffHint, and cli/sir/sir-parse.mjs GLUE; pinned authority
  selfhost/.authority/6199e2cc8b75; seam selfhost/seams/diff_hint.mjs. Re-cut 2026-10-27 for round 5 (FINDINGS #95), round 5b
  (FINDINGS #115).
